只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Telegram bridge for DeepSeek Harness: text, voice, photos and project-per-topic sessions without opening the desktop app","id":"gh:1432964548","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-tg-bridge","slug":"aleksvega/dsh-tg-bridge","topics":["ai-agent","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","telegram","telegram-bot"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Telegram bridge for DeepSeek Harness: text, voice, photos and project-per-topic sessions without ope"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ning the desktop app"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-tg-bridge"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Drive DeepSeek Harness from Telegram. It runs on the\nmachine that already has the harness, and it an"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"swers in the chat where you asked."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A forum topic is a project: its own session, working directory, model,\npermissions and language. Two"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" topics share the install and nothing else."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Never made a bot? QUICKSTART.md goes from \"no account\" to a bot\nthat answers, one step at a time."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **A model per topic.** `/model` lists the routes the profile declares — provider\nand model togethe"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"r — and a tap switches this topic only. `/model <route> all`\nmoves the default the other topics foll"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"ow; `/model auto` hands the topic back.\nA chat for thinking out loud and a chat for engineering no l"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"onger share one model.\n- **A topic is a project.** `/cd my-app`, and every turn runs from that direc"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"tory —\non a permission-enabled profile the sandbox is narrowed to it too, so the agent\ncannot write "},{"id":"p7s6","text":"outside the project.\n- **One edited message per turn.** Steps, a timer and the cache hit rate, plus "},{"id":"p7s7","text":"the\nreasoning in a collapsed block you can tap open. A long turn adds a second\ncollapsed block with "},{"id":"p7s8","text":"every tool call. `/stop` is a button on that message.\n- **`/diff` — review the turn, one hunk at a t"},{"id":"p7s9","text":"ime.** The working tree is split into\nfiles and hunks; every hunk gets two buttons: explain it, or r"},{"id":"p7s10","text":"evert just that\nhunk. A button carries a hash of the hunk it was drawn from, so a press that\narrives"},{"id":"p7s11","text":" after the file moved on is refused instead of touching a line nobody was\nlooking at. `/diff stat` i"},{"id":"p7s12","text":"s the file list alone.\n- **An endpoint from the chat.** `/endpoint add <id> <https://url/v1> <KEY_EN"},{"id":"p7s13","text":"V>\n[model,model]` writes the provider without an AI turn, and the key itself is\nnever typed — only t"},{"id":"p7s14","text":"he name of the variable that holds it. The new models appear\non `/model` as routes.\n- **Input: text,"},{"id":"p7s15","text":" voice, photos.** Any speech engine plugs in — a local script, any\ncommand-line tool, or an OpenAI-c"},{"id":"p7s16","text":"ompatible API (see `docs/VOICE.md`)\n— and the transcript is shown before the answer. A photo is read"},{"id":"p7s17","text":" by the turn's own\nmodel through `read_image`, text and UI included; no second model is needed.\n- **"},{"id":"p7s18","text":"Goal and checklist per topic.** `/goal`, `/tasks`; both survive restarts and\nare prepended to every "},{"id":"p7s19","text":"turn.\n- **Two scopes for every setting.** `/reasoning <mode> all` moves the default,\nwithout `all` i"},{"id":"p7s20","text":"t moves this topic; language and pinning follow the same rule,\nand `/crew use reviewer` gives one to"},{"id":"p7s21","text":"pic its own effort, permissions and agent\npreset (four built-in sets, read-only, copyable).\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## First run"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"`setup.mjs` leaves a working bridge with these defaults, and none of them need\na decision before the"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ves a working bridge with these defaults, and none of them need\na decision before the first message:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Setting | Default | Where to change it |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| profile | `headless` | `/profile` |\n| folder | the workspace you ran setup in | `/cd` |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- Node.js ≥ 24 (the version DeepSeek Harness ships; sessions are zstd-compressed)\n- DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" `0.2.1-rc.2` or newer in the `0.2.x` line (`>=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0`)\n- DeepSeek Harness installed (`~/"},{"id":"p13s3","text":".dsh/profiles/headless`)\n- A Telegram bot token from @BotFather"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The supported harness range is declared in `engines.dsh`; that field decides\ncompatibility on its ow"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"n (DSH ignores `peerDependencies` when it is present).\nThe range includes an explicit prerelease bra"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"nch, because a plain `<0.3.0`\nsilently excludes `0.2.2-*` builds. A future `0.3.0` needs an explicit"},{"id":"p14s4","text":" bump:\nthe bridge relies on the `0.2.x` CLI flags and profile layout."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### What it needs from DSH"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"The bridge is a client of the DSH CLI, and the surface it uses is small enough to\nwrite down: `--pro"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"file`, `--json`, `--session-id`, `--expose-internals <cli.js>`\nwhen the app binary runs the CLI, and"},{"id":"p16s3","text":" the `{\"type\": ...}` JSON events on stdout.\nProfiles are read as files (`cordis.patch.yml`, `package"},{"id":"p16s4","text":".json`) under\n`~/.dsh/profiles`. `package.json` spells the supported range out in\n`engines.dsh`, and"},{"id":"p16s5","text":" it is capped below `0.3.0` on purpose: a minor bump may rename\nan event, and a bridge that guesses "},{"id":"p16s6","text":"is a bridge that answers with silence."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Two escape hatches, for a moved app or a DSH that ships differently:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"`/doctor` prints the command a turn would actually run, so a machine where these\nmatter says so inst"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"ead of failing with an empty answer."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"**As a DSH plugin** (the package carries a `dsh.bundle`; the catalog entry is\npending review):"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"The plugin starts one bridge when DSH boots and stops it on shutdown; if a\nbridge is already running"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" (for example from the scheduled task), it leaves it\nalone. Run `npx dsh-tg-bridge@latest init ...` "},{"id":"p22s3","text":"first so a config exists."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"What `init` does:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| What | Where |"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"| bot token | `~/.dsh/.credentials.yaml` → `refs.DSH_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`; other keys are left alone "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"|\n| your id and working directory | `~/.dsh/tg-bridge/config.json`; an existing file is not overwrit"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"ten |\n| `headless` profile | checked, with a hint on how to create it if missing |"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"`init` flags: `--cwd <path>` (default `~/Projects`), `--voice` (enable\nvoice transcription), `--dry-"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"run` (show what would be written, change nothing)."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Optional provider settings live in `config.json`:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"| Key | Meaning |"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"| `providerKeys` | extra env var names to pass to a turn, read from `~/.dsh/.credentials.yaml`; defa"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ult `[]` |\n| `pricesUrl` | retired: `/prices` always reads OpenRouter's public list and labels the n"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"umber as a reference for the model |\n| `vision.patch` | opt-in overlay profile for photo turns; defa"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"ult `\"\"` — the turn's own model reads images |\n| `vision.enabled` | set `true` to run photo turns on"},{"id":"p29s5","text":" `vision.patch` instead of the topic profile |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The bridge is a single process with long polling. Each turn spawns a separate\nCLI process that exits"},{"id":"p32s2","text":" after the answer, so \"no DSH process\" between\nturns is normal, not a failure."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"- `config.json`, `state.json`, `pending/`, logs are in `.gitignore` and never\nend up in the reposito"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"ry.\n- The token is stored in the DSH credentials store, not in code or config.\n- The bridge only rep"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"lies to ids in `allowedUserIds`."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"},{"content":"上次校验失败；重新生成完整对象。evidence本次只选1至2条，每个编号必须从实际输入列表复制，不得推算或补造编号。保持摘要简洁，limitations最多3条。错误：["output_not_object","output_not_object","finish_reason"]","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
